		{
			"id":"6f8380beab67c98b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"ANTHURIUM should use a mix of SNES-sounding instruments and techniques with more modern sounding instruments.\n\nnew title screen track\n\tvaried, interesting (there will be periods of time that this track will be playing nonstop for minutes)\n\tmotif?\n    \ntwo main tracks for gameplay\n\ttracks should be split into layers (DRUMS, BASS, CHORDS, MELODY, PAD, LEAD, VOCALS)???\n\tat the beginning of the game, there are 2 layers playing.\n\tas the anthurium grows in size (esoterica in magnitude), additional layers will increase in volume.\n\t\nbloom song!\n\tcrazy stuff is happening here, so the song should sound chaotic but not tuneless\n\n(undecided if i even want) game over song (30 seconds, then the title screen track will begin playing again)\n\tthe player has just died, possibly after hours of playing.\n\nundecided on sound profile for ANTHURIUM!\n\n\ntribal percussion\nbitcrush\nearthbound soundfont\nreally close reverb/delay\nfretless bass",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2780,
			"y":-260,
