		{
			"id":"2a1027d88103d458",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"add ability/hud support for MODIFIER key\n\nhud smartly switching ability icons when MODIFIER key is held down\n\nability will have to have two different icons as well\n\ndefine a fallback texture for no icon",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4120,
			"y":-650,
			"width":460,
			"height":210
		},
		{
			"id":"54af69f0cd6ae0a0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"get z-axis working\n\n#### okay\n- [x] z-axis needs to connect to hitbox and change its layer based on z-axis value\n- [x] z-axis must connect to ability manager\n- [x] ability should have a field `affected by z-axis`\n- [x] so that abilities that have hurtboxes can change hurtbox layer based on z-axis\n- [x] physicscomponent needs to connect to z-axis; collisions should not happen between entities that are 5 z units apart (?)\n\n- [x] z-axis needs a reference to sprite `scale` to generate a shadow of a particular size\n- [x] shadow should decrease in size the higher up z value is\n\n- [ ] jumping over terrain\n\n- [x] shadows\n- [x] jumping\n\n- [x] verify that the hitbox/hurtbox levels work by making a flying entity",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-650,
			"width":590,
			"height":510
		},
		{
			"id":"701228c35defd60d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"actual competent entityspawner mechanic:\nentities won't be spawned using their name directly, instead entities will use the entitytag system to define an esoterica archetype for the entity!\n\n> done 09-01-2026\n\nso we made these changes\n- made the registries!\n\t- `EntityRegistry` got fitted with new code that indexes all registered enemies and organizes them into categories based on their `CreatureArchetype`.\n\t- `AccessoryArchetypeRegistry` which registers all `AccessoryArchetypes`, needed for the Anthurium to pick which accessory to grow based on its current `Esoterica` value.\n- `SpawnTable` resource defines weights for each category in `CreatureArchetype` and utilizes the `EntityRegistry` to pick an entity id (`StringName`) based on a weighted intersection of all the categories.\n\t- `SpawnTableSpawnerComponent` holds a `SpawnTable` and calls its function.\n- `spawn_portal(pos: Vector2, spawn_table: SpawnTable)` is now a method in `EntityManager`",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":320,
			"y":-665,
			"width":500,
			"height":540
		},
		{
			"id":"5337b9a1c263e641",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"a main menu\n\nthe main menu should just be an already initialized game without the player\n\n(the camera should choose to focus on a randomly picked entity on the map)\n\nthere will only be an option to play again or turn on and off the shaders. (this is because this will be a demo copy)\n\n> done 09-04-2026\n\n---\n\n- [x] it is written in `AppController` `enum AppStatus { MENU, GAME, GAMEOVER }`.\n- [x] **MENU** should have the main menu open and visible with hand visible and able to select various interactableui elements.\n- [x] title, play, shader settings. (this is a demo copy so no quit button)\n\nmake this:\n- UIStage (simply registers all of its interactableUI)\n\t- InteractableUI (multiple of these, triggers an event when the hand activates it)\n\nwhere a method on `Hand` `switch_to_stage(stage: UIStage)` correctly moves the hand to the first element in the stage. this will be useful for navigating through different menu screens.\n\nessentially, activate a new game but do not spawn the player.\n\nensure that the hand always follows the element in space that it has selected.\n\n**GAME** is when the player is spawned and fully in control.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":320,
			"y":-75,
			"width":710,
			"height":680
		},
		{
			"id":"6f8380beab67c98b",
